--- Decide the one net move for a stock rule-group at the open tier.
-- 
--   - `backpackCount < selfTarget` ⇒ WITHDRAW the deficit, bounded by what the
--     open storage physically holds. Never deposits.
--   - `backpackCount > selfTarget` ⇒ DEPOSIT the excess, clamped to the tier's
--     remaining account-wide capacity when capped. Never withdraws.
--   - `backpackCount == selfTarget` ⇒ NONE (fixpoint).
-- 
-- The deficit/excess are mutually exclusive over one frozen `backpackCount`, so
-- the result is single-signed by construction — the structural defense against
-- the 2-cycle. Both branches are bounded so the post-move count never crosses
-- `selfTarget`, guaranteeing the strict L1 decrease.
function ____exports.planStockReconcile(snap)
    local deficit = snap.selfTarget - snap.backpackCount
